# Subsystem architecture

## Responsibility and owner

State the subsystem's responsibility and the owner of its authoritative state.

Give its main location and useful scene, script or resource reading entries, linking an existing module README where sufficient. Link relevant verification entries when useful; keep test details in their existing records. This navigation remains useful even when the optional runtime-flow section is omitted.

## Boundaries and allowed dependencies

Identify key actual direct collaborators and what the subsystem uses them for. Distinguish these from permitted dependency directions; explain why the boundaries exist and any approved exceptions. Link back to `../architecture.md`.

Summarize key reasons needed to understand the current subsystem and link existing Feature design/notes or ADRs for detail. Preserve historical decisions in their owning records; do not invent missing rationale or create an ADR just to fill this map.

## Key runtime flows (optional)

Describe flows whose ordering, ownership or failure behavior matters across modules. Trace the trigger, participating modules, authoritative state change and observable result, with links to the relevant implementation. Use a short sequence or diagram only when it helps explain the flow.

Include the details that affect this subsystem:

- Where Node, Resource, SceneTree or file I/O enters the flow, and where domain logic stays independent of the engine.
- Who creates and owns runtime state, resources and subscriptions, and who releases or cancels them on completion, scene exit or interruption.
- Where failure is detected and handled, what remains valid, and how failure or recovery reaches the caller or presentation.

Distinguish observed behavior from proposed or unverified flows. Inspect the actual call path; dynamic signals and loading may require runtime verification. Link interface definitions, implementation plans and tests in their existing records. Omit this section when the flow is already clear from local code.

## Reliable extracted facts

Link optional generated facts with extractor, snapshot and scope. They do not replace the human-owned responsibility and dependency contract above.

## Maintenance

Follow the Navigation and Maintaining a map sections of `methodology/10-architecture-overview.md` for content, change triggers and checks.
